    "body": "`feature_anchors.py` builds the expected `anchors.dat` substring from each peer's port with `hex(port)[2:]`, which is not zero-padded. The port is serialized as two bytes, so for ports below 4096 the expected string is one hex digit short and `assert ip_port in anchors_hex` fails.\n\nThis only shows up with a non-default port range, for example when avoiding local listeners:\n\n```\nTEST_RUNNER_PORT_MIN=1100 test/functional/feature_anchors.py\n```\n\nfails on master with `AssertionError` at the `assert ip_port in anchors_hex` line and passes with this change; the default range still passes.\n\n\n\n---\nDisclosure: AI (Claude Fable 5.1) was used to find this issue and to draft this PR.\n",
